# cr-04 done: shared workspace relay for the Craft apps

Generalised the fc-02 Video Studio relay into one neutral `workspaceRelay` that
also drives the five Loam Craft editors (docs/sheets/slides/photo/design), with
the video exports kept as backward-compatible aliases.

## Server (commit cd55aae, tests ff543ac)
- `src/server/workspaceRelay.ts`: targets `film|effects|docs|sheets|slides|photo|design`,
  `isCraftTarget()`, errors `PANEL_NOT_OPEN | TIMEOUT | CANCELLED | COMMAND_REJECTED`,
  one command at a time per **task+target** FIFO queue, per-command timeout
  (default 120 s, `LOAM_WORKSPACE_RELAY_TIMEOUT_MS` / legacy
  `LOAM_VIDEO_STUDIO_TIMEOUT_MS`), `isAttached()`, `pendingCount()`, `enqueue()`,
  `resolve()`, `cancelTask()`, `takeOpenRequest()` (one-shot, craft only) and
  `openRequestsFor()` (SSE replay). Publishes `workspace_command` and
  `workspace_open_request`; video targets keep publishing the legacy
  `video_studio_command` event type.
- `src/server/videoStudioRelay.ts` is now a thin re-export shim.
- `src/agent/events.ts`, `src/graph/runGraph.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` updated
  (result route accepts `/api/tasks/:id/workspace/result` next to the
  `/video-studio/result` alias).

## Web (commit 4202a73)
- `packages/web/src/lib/relayClientBase.ts`: shared stream half (SSE fetch,
  frame decode, dispatch, POST result, reconnect, open-request reporting).
- `packages/web/src/lib/craftRelayClient.ts`: Craft targets on the neutral
  `workspace_command` event + `/workspace/result` route, plus the relay
  pseudo-methods:
  - `craft.open` fetches the task file and drops it into the editor iframe
    (`{type:'craft:open', name, bytes}`), so the app behaves like a dropped file;
  - `craft.waitSave` runs `file.save` (or any save/export command), waits for the
    `craft:save` upload and resolves with the stored task-file path.
  Every other method goes straight to the bridge (`engine.execute` / `call`), so
  the agent tool can reach the whole control protocol.
- `packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.ts` extends the shared base and keeps
  the legacy event type and result route unchanged; `VideoStudioRelay` /
  `videoStudioRelay` aliases remain.
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/craft/CraftPanel.tsx` exports the
  save/mime helpers the relay reuses, so a `waitSave` stores exactly what the
  panel's own Save button would.

## Tests
- Server: `src/server/__tests__/workspaceRelay.test.ts` (craft enqueue->result,
  per task+target independence, FIFO, TIMEOUT/CANCELLED/COMMAND_REJECTED,
  PANEL_NOT_OPEN + one-shot open request + SSE replay, legacy event type) and the
  existing `videoStudioRelay.test.ts` / `videoStudioE2E.test.ts`.
- Web: `packages/web/src/lib/craftRelayClient.test.ts` (craft dispatch to a mocked
  CraftBridge, `craft.waitSave` resolves with the uploaded path, `craft.open`,
  open-request reporting, legacy video frames ignored, no-panel error result) and
  the existing `videoStudioClient.test.ts` / `CraftPanel.test.tsx`.

## Gates (all green from the worktree root)
1. `npx tsc --noEmit`
2. `npm run build:server`
3. `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`
4. `node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/workspaceRelay.test.ts src/server/__tests__/videoStudioRelay.test.ts src/server/__tests__/videoStudioE2E.test.ts`
   -> 23 tests pass
   `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)` -> 479 tests pass (73 files)

## Commits
- cd55aae cr-04(server): generalise the video studio relay into a shared workspace relay
- ff543ac cr-04(test): cover the generalised workspace relay
- 4202a73 cr-04(web): drive the Craft apps through the shared workspace relay

## Notes / follow-ups
- The `workspace_open_request` is reported to the host through
  `CraftRelayClientOptions.onOpenRequest`; the shell auto-open handler itself is
  cr-03 (not in this branch) and is intentionally out of scope here.
- `packages/shared/src/socket.ts` has no `workspace_command` / `video_studio_command`
  members, so `EventList.tsx` needs no new cases: these are live-only relay
  signals, not chat events (matching `src/graph/runGraph.ts`).
